{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration/recovery policy in specifications. The policy gives one clear controllable action per decision/recovery state, keeps all uncontrollable events defined in every spec state, treats obstacle events as safety-critical preemptions in action states, prefers forward progress in clear conditions, uses brief directed turns for ordinary recovery, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated last-resort stuck state reached only after repeated front blockage.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensor outcomes from motion-actuation capability in G so E can impose safe event-to-action bindings cleanly.",
    "Bias toward coverage by making clear/path_clear lead to move_forward, using random_walk only as a secondary exploration mode after a forward pulse, using directed turns for side/front obstacles, and using move_backward and full_rotate only in dedicated recovery chains."
  ],
